- For each combination of placements of A and B (≤ 10,000 total), represent each cut-out row as a bitmask: A's row masks shifted by its column offset, OR-ed with B's. The cut-out matches X iff for every row `(A_mask | B_mask) == X_mask`. This guarantees every black square lands on a `#` of X and every `#` of X is covered (overlaps allowed).

