**Key points:**
- Only black squares must be inside the cut-out window; transparent parts can hang outside, so offsets are bounded via black-square extents (the offset ranges are also empty automatically if black squares can't fit, correctly yielding "No").
- Negative shifts (sheet extending past the window's left/top) are handled with right-shifts; no bits are lost because the offset ranges guarantee black squares stay in `[0, wX-1]` / `[0, hX-1]`.
- Row mask equality checks both directions: no black square on a transparent cell of X, and no `#` of X left uncovered.

